s on all the reasons why it  sucked and try to give some  encouragement and say hey  these things are really great let's  continue to improve here and here's how  you can get better  expect imperfection if they see your  face like  if i'm on the sidelines doing this as  alex is teaching it's over he's lost  he's lost his confidence he's not going  to do it anymore and it's not even just  not expressing it it's not feeling it  i expect it if he fell on his face for  that move that he wanted me to go off  and teach it would be okay  everything is savable i expect  imperfections  and if you're throwing people into new  opportunities you should too  communication is one of the most  important skills that entrepreneurs need  to have and i think a lot of businesses  fail because the entrepreneur cannot  communicate well and if  they even are sharing their ideas they  are not  convincing enough and so a lot of great  ideas die  you could have the next greatest idea  that can change the world it's sitting  up here  but because you can't articulate it  because you can't share it because you  can't communicate it well and because  you're not convincing enough  to the people around you it will never  take off the idea will die within you  and i hate that  i hate that because building a business  getting the thing that's out here out  into the world is greater than one  person  no matter how much of a genius you are  to build a business you need a team  you need a team of people to help you go  far and you also need to convince  the media and customers and partners and  suppliers that what you have  is amazing if you are the only one who  thinks that your idea  is amazing and you can't communicate or  convince anybody else of that  then you're done then that idea dies  within you and i think unfortunately  that's a lot of entrepreneurs so jordan  has three of his tips i'm gonna give you  three of mine on how to be a convincing  communicator  step number one is have a powerful  